# Boundaries & dependencies

## Bounded contexts
- Identity
- SocialGraph
- Content
- Messaging (DMs)
- ActivityPub
- Blockchain (Monad)
- Moderation
- Media

## Dependency rules
- Modules do NOT import internal files from other modules.
- Cross-module interaction happens via:
  1) exported ports/interfaces (stable)
  2) domain events
  3) jobs for async work

## “Direct calls” allowed (v1)
- Direct function calls across modules are allowed ONLY through exported ports.
- Never reach into another module’s Prisma models directly.

## Enforce a thin edge
- GraphQL resolvers and HTTP controllers do:
  - authn/authz
  - input validation
  - call command/query handler
  - map result to API shape
- No business logic in resolvers/controllers.

## Naming conventions
- Commands: imperative verbs (`PublishPost`, `FollowUser`, `SendMessage`)
- Queries: nouns/questions (`GetHomeFeed`, `GetThread`, `SearchUsers`)
